  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">HEAD OUT TOGETHER: a hip surgery training action</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The overall objective of the project is to improve the quality of public health services in Eritrea, specifically in the field of Paediatric Orthopaedics, by providing expertise to enable healthcare staff to make accurate early diagnoses to reduce the impact of DDH (Developmental Dysplasia of the Hip) in Eritrean infants and children. This will lead to the prevention of deformities caused by undiagnosed hip dysplasia and, consequently, facilitate the treatment of this condition at all stages.</narrative>
  </description>
